bs have embraced and accepted our values of openness, community, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL155: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? cite43†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org .\nL156: \nL157: cite44†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite45†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL158: \nL159: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite46†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL160: cite47†About†info.arxiv.org · cite48†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite51†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite52†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite53†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite54†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L161: \nL162: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2007.09024] Perturbation Bounds for (Nearly) Orthogonally Decomposable Tensors (https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.09024)\nciteturn0view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.09024\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 167\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Numerical Analysis\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 17 Jul 2020 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 21 Jan 2022 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:Perturbation Bounds for (Nearly) Orthogonally Decomposable Tensors\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Arnab Auddy , cite7†Ming Yuan L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Perturbation Bounds for (Nearly) Orthogonally Decomposable Tensors, by Arnab Auddy and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We develop deterministic perturbation bounds for singular values and vectors of orthogonally decomposable tensors, in a spirit similar to classical results for matrices such as those due to Weyl, Davis, Kahan and Wedin. Our bounds demonstrate intriguing differences between matrices and higher-order tensors.\nL17: Most notably, they indicate that for higher-order tensors perturbation affects each essential singular value/vector in isolation, and its effect on an essential singular vector does not depend on the multiplicity of its corresponding singular value or its distance from other singular values. Our results can be readily applied and provide a unified treatment to many different problems in statistics and machine learning involving spectral learning of higher-order orthogonally decomposable tensors.\nL18: In particular, we illustrate the implications of our bounds in the context of high dimensional tensor SVD problem, and how it can be used to derive optimal rates of convergence for spectral learning.\nL19: Subjects:  | Numerical Analysis (math.NA); Statistics Theory (math.ST); Machine Learning (stat.ML)\nL20: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 15A18, 15A69, 47J10, 49M27, 49R05, 62H25\nL21: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2007.09024 [math.NA]\nL22:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2007.09024v2 [math.NA] for this version)\nL23:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2007.09024†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Arnab Auddy [cite13†view email ]\nL27: cite5†[v1] Fri, 17 Jul 2020 14:34:58 UTC (36 KB)\nL28: [v2] Fri, 21 Jan 2022 15:10:55 UTC (284 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Perturbation Bounds for (Nearly) Orthogonally Decomposable Tensors, by Arnab Auddy and 1 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite8†View PDF L37:   * cite9†HTML (experimental